<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Cast</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>cast &lt;spell&gt; [&lt;target&gt;]
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>cast magic missile orc
cast cure light wounds Gnort
cast mag mis           (at whoever you are fighting)
cast bless             (on yourself)
</pre>
<p>Casts a spell you have learned, of magic or of divine power (see 
<a cmd='#'>Help Magic</a>). Name the spell, then whom or what it is for. Leave out the 
target, and an attack spell goes at whoever you are fighting, and a 
helping spell mostly at yourself.
</p><p>You can shorten each word of the spell's name: cast mag mis is magic 
missile. Take care not to shorten too much: cur could be cure or curse, 
and that can be quite a bad mistake.
</p><p>Every spell costs mana (see <a cmd='#'>Help Mana Points</a>): without enough, you can't 
summon enough energy to cast it. Most spells need you to stand; some can 
be cast in a fight, and a few resting or even lying wounded. Those around you hear 
the words you utter. In a fight, a spell takes time, like a blow.
</p><p>How well it works depends on your skill in the spell, your magic or 
divine ability and your skill in its sphere (see <a cmd='#'>Help Spheres</a>); and 
many spells can be resisted. <a cmd='#'>status spells</a> shows the spells you know, and 
each spell has its own help: help and the spell's name.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Spheres</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Magic</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Mana Points</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Practice</a>
</pre>




</div>